# Arcade Integration Rules

See ADR-0010. Prefer SDK over hand-rolled HTTP (also `AGENTS.md` §3a).

## SDK & client

- `@arcadeai/arcadejs` is imported ONLY from `lib/arcade/**`. App code uses
  typed wrappers in `lib/arcade/tools.ts`, `authorize.ts`, `catalog.ts`, etc.
- **Prefer Arcade SDK → REST → MCP** over raw `fetch`, doc scraping, or parallel
  HTTP clients. When no primitive exists (no `/v1/toolkits` today), paginate
  `client.tools.list()` and document the gap — see `lib/arcade/catalog.ts`.
- Singleton client via `lib/arcade/client.ts`. App-level cache + inflight dedup
  is allowed; reimplementing wire protocol is not.

## Identity

- All Arcade `user_id` values go through `lib/arcade/identity.ts`.
- **`ARCADE_VERIFIER_MODE=arcade`** (recommended single-project default): personal
  OAuth uses the operator email so Arcade's built-in user verifier matches the
  arcade.dev session. Shared connections are disabled — they require custom verifier.
- **`ARCADE_VERIFIER_MODE=custom`** (multi-project / production-only): personal →
  `user:{betterAuthUserId}`, shared → `workspace:{workspaceId}`. Never pass raw
  email as Arcade `user_id` in this mode. Requires a **dedicated Arcade project
  per environment** because the Dashboard's verifier URL setting is project-global.

## OAuth & verifier

- Start OAuth via `lib/arcade/authorize.ts` (`tools.authorize`). `authorizeToolkit`
  MUST NOT pass `next_uri` to Arcade — Arcade rejects arbitrary return URIs in
  both verifier modes. Post-OAuth return is stored per-row via `oauth_return_to`.
- **Single-project setup (default):** Arcade Dashboard → Auth → User Verifier
  stays on **Arcade default** (no custom URL). Set `ARCADE_VERIFIER_MODE=arcade`
  in every environment. Operator email is the Arcade `user_id`.
- **Multi-project setup (opt-in):** dedicated prod Arcade project with Custom
  verifier URL `${BETTER_AUTH_URL}/api/arcade/verify`. `/api/arcade/verify` calls
  `auth.confirmUser` via `lib/arcade/verifier.ts`. Set `ARCADE_VERIFIER_MODE=custom`
  only in that environment.

## OAuth UX (Connect / Authorize buttons)

- Open the auth URL in a **new tab** via `window.open(url, '_blank')`. Do not
  redirect the current tab — the user loses unsaved state and the parent never
  observes completion.
- Listeners on `visibilitychange` + `focus` flag an awaiting-auth `useRef` and
  trigger a single `GET /api/connections` (or intent fetch) on return. Reference
  implementations: `components/connections/connections-client.tsx`,
  `components/intent/intent-side-panel.tsx`.
- `GET /api/connections` calls `syncPendingConnections` to re-check Arcade for
  `pending` / `unknown` rows and mark them `completed` if the grant is live.
  Do not duplicate this scan in components.

## Scoped revocation

- OAuth scopes are granted at the **provider** level, not the toolkit level. To
  "remove one toolkit" without nuking the rest of a provider family:
  1. `revokeUserConnection()` (calls `admin.userConnections.list` + `.delete`)
     to drop the provider grant.
  2. `resetConnectionAfterRevoke()` on the removed toolkit row.
  3. Re-`tools.authorize` each other toolkit sharing that provider; if any
     comes back with an `auth_url`, return it as `reauthorizeUrl` so the UI
     reopens OAuth for the user.
- Provider family is normalized via `providerFamily()` (handles `arcade-*`
  prefixes). Reference: `app/api/connections/[toolkit]/route.ts` DELETE handler.

## Connections & execution

- `toolkit_connections.scope`: `personal` | `shared` with partial unique indexes
  (see migration `0001_connection_scope.sql`).
- Before execute, `lib/aig/executor.ts` MUST:
  1. `resolveConnectionForTool()` for the approver + toolkit
  2. `validateConnectionForExecution()` in pure `lib/aig/connection-auth.ts`
- Failures surface as `AIGBlockedAuthError`.
- Shared connection management gated by `canManageSharedConnections()`.

## Tool definitions & catalog

- Use `client.tools.formatted.list({ format: 'anthropic', toolkit, user_id })`.
  Do not hand-wrap tool schemas.
- Connections page: curated list via parallel `tools.list({ toolkit })`; full
  search index via paginated `tools.list({ user_id })` with 30-min cache.
- Admin operations (provider revoke, provider list) go through
  `client.admin.*` — never raw HTTP.

## Security & testing

- Never log API keys. Pino redacts `ARCADE_API_KEY` and `*.apiKey`.
- Mock client (`lib/arcade/mock.ts`, `E2E_MOCK_ARCADE=1`) MUST match real client
  types so executor cannot distinguish at compile time.
